<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jezzailchi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as jezzailchis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jezzailchis were soldiers armed with the jezail, a long-barrelled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">musket</a> used in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> employed mounted infantry armed with firearms who could dismount to deliver accurate musket fire and then remount for pursuit. These troops were a notable tactical innovation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a>'s army.</p></div>
